C MP+relacq
"Message passing with a release store and an acquire load -- the strongest shape
 CRC can express, since CRC's fragment is non-atomic + release/acquire +
 SC-fences and deliberately OMITS relaxed atomics (to sidestep thin-air). The
 release/acquire pair builds happens-before from the data write to the data read,
 so the stale-data outcome r0=1 /\ r1=0 is a coherence violation: CRC FORBIDS it,
 and so does flat C11 on this annotation. herd7 -c11 => Never. This is the CRC
 (stronger) side; the C11 (weaker) side is the relaxed companion MP+relaxed.litmus,
 which CRC cannot even write down and C11 allows."
{ int x=0; int f=0; }
P0 (int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  *x = 1;
  atomic_store_explicit(f,1,memory_order_release);
}
P1 (int* x, atomic_int* f) {
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(f,memory_order_acquire);
  int r1 = *x;
}
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=0)
